{"agent_id":"pp3g-bGeK-complete-the-hy3-review-of-the-workflow-topology-ba69","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-07T23:19:36.109348849Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"35c2be3c-b5f4-4d9a-9272-a3bb703d6600","comment_uuid":"7a1a5748-5e97-41a6-8f42-0727d5f89191","author":"pp3g-bGeK-complete-the-hy3-review-of-the-workflow-topology-ba69","content":"VERDICT PART 1/4 (hy3, edge-case/source lens) -- WORKFLOW-TOPOLOGY PROPOSAL (#241).\n\nHEADLINE: CONDITIONAL PASS. The proposal is directionally correct and its two principles are genuinely load-bearing, but it is stated one abstraction level above the stack it must land on, and three of its mechanical preconditions are currently FALSE in this repo. 12 numbered findings across 4 axes; 8 blocking conditions in Part 4/4.\n\nBASIS: preserved analysis from #242 [VERIFY] and #247 [PROGRESS]. Every citation below was spot-confirmed live this session unless explicitly marked 'preserved'. Posted in chunks because this verdict was lost to a 504 streaming error twice.\n\nAXIS 1 -- THE TWO PRINCIPLES (source-fidelity lens).\n\nF1 [HIGH] PRINCIPLE (b) DRIFTS FROM ITS SOURCE, AND THE DRIFT IS ITSELF THE FAILURE MODE. Source re-derived verbatim at syntheses/2026-06-23-beds24-booking-system-evolution.md:39 -- 'Rule #2: Cheapest Falsifying Test First: Before writing complex code, execute the absolute cheapest test that can prove the core premise wrong.' The proposal restates this as the cheapest DISCRIMINATING test. Falsifying -> discriminating is a substantive weakening, not a paraphrase: a discriminating test merely separates two hypotheses, so an agent satisfies it with a cheap CONFIRMING check aimed at the premise it wants to be true. This is not academic pedantry -- the hub record contains the exact failure. In #226 -> #231 the marker-grep 'discriminated' (marker present vs absent) while wholly failing to falsify 'the build actually works'. The source rule would have caught it; the restated rule licenses it. Restore the source word.\n\nF2 [MEDIUM] PRINCIPLE (a) IS FAITHFUL BUT HAS NO CARRIER. It tracks its sources correctly (Core System Prompt v1/v2 reasoning standards; AGENTS.md evidence vs interpretation vs finding vs recommendation), and its 'state what was NOT tested' clause is a genuine ADDITION beyond source -- negative-space disclosure is the strongest single idea in the proposal. But the crosslink comment vocabulary is fixed and closed: note, plan, decision, observation, blocker, resolution, result, handoff, human (confirmed live). None encodes certainty. So principle (a) can only live in unstructured prose: unenforceable, unparseable, and -- critically -- not mechanically consumable by the model-agreement collection in Axis 4.","created_at":"2026-08-07T23:19:36.102405195Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:eY/brbXhEq7ai6H7oZOD+kB9yAWv+gXPpL4E1iMe0ZA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgIcnsvrSqCctqGKfM7z9KDRMoMxSAXlfLD6+rFag/5H0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA/iKwNZcvId7EjAHwqfysP/r6mpRRgmf72wdnLxdsWKn8etyEp9ErsMB6jUlxw7h5Xeaq/c8fMtLGucIDSkc+Ag=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:eY/brbXhEq7ai6H7oZOD+kB9yAWv+gXPpL4E1iMe0ZA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgIcnsvrSqCctqGKfM7z9KDRMoMxSAXlfLD6+rFag/5H0AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNwHoRGYtbh7PjmA6jccPV9a7T2qjDe497O0R6TerlyOASleeQQDssfjMLUAUdvtOdiSCOS6Pp0JhWUHnNgy8QI="}
